### 1. Health check 200 means successful read
GET http://localhost:8081/api/health

### 2. Get all course offerings
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings

### 3. Get a specific course offering that exists
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings/CO001

### 4. Get a course that doesnt exist
GET http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings/C999

### 5. Create a new course offering
POST http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseTitle": "Spring Boot Essentials",
  "instructorName": "Mr Kumar",
  "startDate": "2026-08-01",
  "capacity": 15
}

### 6. Create an invalid course offering
POST http://localhost:8081/api/course-offerings
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseTitle": "",
  "instructorName": "",
  "startDate": "",
  "capacity": 0
}

### 7. Get all instructors
GET http://localhost:8081/api/instructors

### 8. Get a specific instructor
GET http://localhost:8081/api/instructors/I001

### 9. Create an instructor
POST http://localhost:8081/api/instructors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ms Wong",
  "specialty": "DevOps",
  "yearsExperience": 5,
  "available": true
}